WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.319 --> 00:00:07.110 align:start position:0%
 
so  justin was my brother  i'm speaking for both my brother and i  and my family  so you hear a lot of people talking  about what a dedicated officer justin  was  about all the good service he did  he loved his job it was all he ever  wanted to do  for him it was a vocation  a calling  but aside from all that  justin was everything to his family  he was juicy or juice man  in light-hearted moments  but only to family and close friends  he was my brother  but so often he was my rock  no matter where i was in the world  i knew that justin was there for me  as he was for so many  when i was abroad and had to come back  to the states to deal with a difficult  situation in dc  justin flew across the country to meet  me there  and stayed just for moral support just  to be there with me  he's done that more than once  he was always there for me  and everyone in our family  whether it was to help with something  lend a sympathetic ear  provide a strong shoulder  or just for a hug  because justin's hugs were magic  he has  been especially important in my life  as a role model for my two sons  his nephew sebastian and asher  i always tell them that i'm raising them  to be good men  good men like their uncle justin and  uncle joshua  because they could have no better role  models  one of the last times i saw justin in  person  he took me aside just to tell me how  proud he was of me  and the job i was doing raising these  young gentlemen  even though he was my little brother  that meant so much to me  but i know that it's not just me  they are who they are  and my brothers and i are who we are  because of family  we have always recognized  how lucky we are  to have the family we have  justin and joshua had a connection  that few people on this earth will ever  experience  while very different  they're also the same in in many ways  the best ways  they often share the same thoughts  i can't tell you how many times they  showed up to something  wearing the same thing  and when they were little  they had their own language before they  learned to speak  justin had a presence about him  that not only commanded respect  but imparted respect  i dare anyone to find a single person  who could say anything bad about justin  even with someone he had a disagreement  with that person would still say that  justin was a good man  he could just de-escalate any situation  just with his natural demeanor  to every officer who knew justin i will  say this  justin's watched  in the physical world over his sons sean  and jacob has ended  now it's up to you to help fill that  role  keep watch over these boys  and be there in the way that their  father cannot  and the same for stacy  justin was so lucky to have found his  other half  and even though their time together  was shorter than it should have been  they both brought each other so much joy  i'm so happy  that my brother got to experience that  kind of love in his life  which was cut way too short  so while physically departed  justin will remain with us in so many  ways  quiet nights under the stars  walking on a trail  hearing a familiar song  visiting a special place  justin will be with us  and even in this unbearable grief  i can close my eyes  and feel justin's hug  and hear his voice  say that it's gonna be okay  at first i wasn't not sure if i could  even stand up here or even make it up  here  but i think with this podium and  my family and and god  i'll be able to say a few words  justin was my son a best friend  another best friend  family of best friends  he was humble  he was my hero  i told him once after we had sat and  talked for a few minutes we shared our  thoughts for the day  and i told him  you're my hero  and justin in his way said  dad just doing my job just doing my job  well  when justin did his job he did it like  he lived his life  honesty  and integrity  and integrity  and again  what everybody says  if you ever got a justin hug  you know y'all done being hugged  david no no little little yeah no man  you got a  hug was talking with his nephews  sebastian and asher  and i don't know who was consoling who  at that time  and i said you know guys you know we  just got to think about  the good times the happy times that we  had with your uncle justin  and they both looked up and they said  but grandpa there were no other times  there were no bad times no unhappy times  all we had was good times with uncle  justin  and so we all i know his squad members  fellow officers  you've had good times  with justin  cherish those times  and never forget him  and thank you all  you

